meta {
  name: Initiate Application Payment (Student)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/payments/applications/{{applicationId}}/initiate
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{studentAccessToken}}
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 201) {
    const data = res.getBody();
    if (data.data && data.data.id) {
      bru.setEnvVar("transactionId", data.data.id);
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Creates a payment order for the application's CURRENT total across every
  course selected so far (primary + any extras) — not just the primary
  course's own fee. 404 if the application doesn't exist or has no
  primary course; 409 if the fee has already been paid.

  Calling this is what locks courses/quota (see Add Course / Withdraw
  Course / Change Course Quota) — from this point on nothing about the
  course selection can change until either payment is confirmed, or this
  attempt fails and the lock releases. Idempotent while a "pending"
  transaction already exists: calling again just returns that same
  transaction rather than creating a duplicate order (safe, since courses
  can't have changed while locked).

  The fee ledger entry (StudentFeeLedger, feeCategory "application_fee")
  is created lazily on first call here — not at Start Application — using
  the application's running total, and refreshed to the current total on
  each call if a previous attempt had failed and the total has since
  changed.

  Behind a PaymentProvider interface (apps/api/src/modules/payments/lib/) —
  today this returns a fabricated order id from a mock provider with no
  real money movement. A real gateway (Razorpay standard, RazorpayX, or
  Razorpay Route) plugs in later as a second implementation of the same
  interface; nothing about this endpoint's contract changes when that
  happens, only what `providerOrderId` actually is.
}
